---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Section from '../../components/ui/Section.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/ui/PageHeader.astro';
import { breadcrumbLd, webPageLd } from '../../config/seo';

const pageDescription =
  'The terms that govern your use of foxelabs.com, our open-source software, paid plugin licenses, and trading tools.';

// Single source of truth for the visible date and the schema's dateModified.
const updatedIso = '2026-08-27';
const updated = new Date(updatedIso + 'T00:00:00Z').toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
  year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC',
});
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | Foxe Labs"
  description={pageDescription}
  jsonLd={[
    breadcrumbLd([
      { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { name: 'Terms of Service', path: '/legal/terms' },
    ]),
    webPageLd({
      name: 'Terms of Service',
      description: pageDescription,
      url: '/legal/terms',
      dateModified: updatedIso,
    }),
  ]}
>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main">
    <PageHeader
      eyebrow="Legal"
      title="Terms of Service"
      lead="The plain-English rules for using our website and software. Short version: use the tools honestly, respect the licenses, and understand what we do and don't promise."
      narrow
    />
    <Section reveal={false}>
      <article class="prose-foxe prose-foxe--doc max-w-3xl">
        <p class="text-[12px]" style="color: var(--ink-dim);">Last updated: {updated}</p>

        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms of Service ("Terms") are an agreement between you and
          <strong>Foxe Labs LLP</strong> ("Foxe Labs", "we", "us"), a limited liability
          partnership based in Kerala, India. They govern your use of
          <a href="/">foxelabs.com</a>, our documentation, our blog, and the software we
          publish — including free open-source releases and paid licenses.
        </p>
        <p>
          By using the site or our software, you accept these Terms. If you don't agree
          with them, please don't use the site or the software.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Our products</h2>
        <p>We ship two kinds of things, and slightly different rules apply to each:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Open-source software</strong> — our WordPress plugins and PHP
            libraries are released under their own open-source licenses (typically
            GPL-2.0-or-later for plugins). The license bundled with each project governs
            how you may use, modify, and redistribute that code. Nothing in these Terms
            restricts the rights those licenses grant you.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Paid licenses and add-ons</strong> — premium versions, add-ons, and
            support plans are sold through our checkout partner
            <a href="https://freemius.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Freemius</a>,
            which acts as the merchant of record. A paid license grants you the right to
            receive updates and support for the covered sites and period you purchased.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Our trading software (expert advisors and trading tools) is sold through the
          MQL5 Market where listed as live (for example, Gold Scalpel); the MQL5 Market's
          own purchase terms apply to those sales. Products still in development are
          available by waitlist only, and product-specific terms will be presented at
          purchase when they launch.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Accounts and license keys</h2>
        <p>
          Paid products may require a license key or a Freemius account to activate
          updates and support. You are responsible for keeping keys confidential. Don't
          share, resell, or publish license keys, and don't use technical tricks to
          activate a license on more sites than it covers.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>When using our site, software, or support channels, you agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>break the law, or use our tools to help someone else break it;</li>
          <li>probe, overload, or attempt to gain unauthorized access to our systems;</li>
          <li>misrepresent our software as your own or strip license and copyright notices where a license requires them;</li>
          <li>use our name, logo, or branding in a way that suggests endorsement we haven't given;</li>
          <li>abuse support — we're a small team, and we help everyone in good faith.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Purchases, billing, and refunds</h2>
        <p>
          Payments are processed by Freemius; we never see or store your card details.
          Prices are shown at checkout and may change for future purchase cycles. Paid
          licenses renew automatically unless you cancel before the renewal date — you
          can cancel any time from your Freemius account, and cancelling stops future
          charges without affecting the current period.
        </p>
        <p>
          Refunds are covered by our <a href="/legal/refunds/">Refund Policy</a> — in
          short, a 7-day no-questions-asked money-back guarantee on paid plugin
          purchases.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Trading software disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Nothing on this site is financial advice.</strong> Our trading tools
          are software utilities, not investment recommendations. Trading foreign
          exchange, CFDs, and other leveraged products carries substantial risk of loss
          and is not suitable for everyone. Past performance — including backtests and
          our own live results — does not guarantee future results. You alone are
          responsible for your trading decisions and for complying with the regulations
          that apply to you.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The Foxe Labs name, logo, site design, and written content are owned by
          Foxe Labs LLP. Open-source code is yours to use under its license. Blog posts
          and documentation may be quoted with attribution and a link; wholesale
          republishing is not permitted.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Warranty disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          Our software is provided <strong>"as is" and "as available"</strong>, without
          warranties of any kind, express or implied — including merchantability,
          fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. We work hard to ship
          reliable software, but we can't promise it will be uninterrupted, error-free,
          or compatible with every environment. Always keep backups and test updates on
          a staging site first.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, Foxe Labs LLP will not be liable for
          any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or exemplary damages —
          including lost profits, lost data, or trading losses — arising from your use
          of the site or software. Our total liability for any claim is limited to the
          amount you paid us for the product giving rise to the claim in the twelve
          months before the claim arose, or ₹1,000 if you paid nothing.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Termination</h2>
        <p>
          We may suspend or terminate access to paid services if you materially breach
          these Terms — for example, by sharing license keys or abusing support. Your
          rights under open-source licenses survive, as those licenses provide.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Changes to these Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms as our products evolve. The "Last updated" date at
          the top reflects the current version. Material changes will be noted on this
          page; continued use after a change means you accept the updated Terms.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by the laws of India. Any dispute will be subject to
          the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of Kerala, India.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these Terms? Email
          <a href="mailto:support@foxelabs.com">support@foxelabs.com</a> or use the
          <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </Section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
